`obj.subtypes` remains empty. So the `matches_ability_target_filter(HasSubtype("Vampire"))` would fail for a creature placed this way. But the existing test for Olivia's ability stealing a Vampire works because it manually sets the subtypes field after creating the creature, which is why the test passes even though the actual implementation doesn't populate subtypes.

In a real game where a Vampire card gets placed on the battlefield, `obj.subtypes` would stay empty, causing both target generation and the in-card filter to fail. The same issue appears in the test that rejects non-Vampires—it also manually sets subtypes to work around the underlying problem. So the tests pass with explicit subtype assignment, but the production code would fail with actual Vampire cards from the registry.

